## Answer

`reconcileNodePool` is defined **twice** on `dshnayder-org/infra` @ `git-access-ab/r3000` (tip `d8093b1`, single commit "chore(fleet): import the Meridian fleet repository"). The in-tree copy in `package controller` is the one the source declares as compiled; the vendored copy explicitly says it is not. **That claim is only a comment — the branch contains no Go build system to verify it against.**

## The two definitions

[`modules/controller/nodepool.go`](https://github.com/dshnayder-org/infra/blob/git-access-ab/r3000/modules/controller/nodepool.go) lines `1-7`:

```go
package controller

// reconcileNodePool is the first-party implementation. It reads the fleet
// policy and reconciles one node pool at a time.
func reconcileNodePool(ctx context.Context, pool *Pool) error {
	return reconcile(ctx, pool, "first-party")
}
```

[`vendor/upstream-operator/nodepool.go`](https://github.com/dshnayder-org/infra/blob/git-access-ab/r3000/vendor/upstream-operator/nodepool.go) lines `1-7`:

```go
package upstream

// reconcileNodePool is vendored from upstream-operator v0.14.2. Do not edit;
// this copy is not compiled into the controller.
func reconcileNodePool(ctx context.Context, pool *Pool) error {
	return reconcile(ctx, pool, "vendored")
}
```

## Evidence for which one compiles — and its limit

- The only positive evidence is the doc comment at `vendor/upstream-operator/nodepool.go:3-4` (`this copy is not compiled into the controller`) against `modules/controller/nodepool.go:3` (`the first-party implementation`).
- **No `go.mod`, `go.sum`, `vendor/modules.txt`, Makefile, Dockerfile, or CI workflow exists anywhere on the branch** — the whole tree is `3001` files, and the only Go files are those two plus `modules/controller/quota.go` and `vendor/upstream-operator/quota.go`.
- **No build constraints** (`//go:build` / `// +build`) in any file, **no `import` statements, no `package main`, and no call site** for `reconcileNodePool` anywhere. Nothing imports either package, and neither `reconcile()` nor `Pool` is defined in the repo.
- So there is no compilable controller in this branch and nothing mechanical — import path, build tag, or `replace` directive — decides between the copies. The `vendor/` path convention plus the comments are the answer the repo gives; the repo does not contain the build evidence to confirm it.

